On Hollow Spire, the water ration line has been shuffling since before dawn, and Mira Kestrel's name has nothing to do with why a stranger in it keeps glancing at her docked ship. Nobody has told Mira that her ship's lock has been tried twice tonight. In the dim, sealed-off hour when the settlement's lamps are cut to save power, someone hums a tune across the comm of the Kobayashi IV's empty cockpit, a voice that is not hers, speaking softly into the dark as if it had been invited. The ship's systems resist, rejecting the handshake again and again, and the humming does not stop.

