The ship's records room is a closet with ambitions, and you are in it, auditing your own reputation. Control, in this case, means arranging the log entries so that every sector's opinion of you reads as slightly more favorable than the sector would admit. A fern sits on the shelf above the console, pressed flat between two sheets of clear film, brown and brittle and kept for reasons the ship's inventory declines to explain. You glance at it each time a log entry turns out to be a stretch. Somewhere in the Cinder Expanse, people are forming opinions of you without your input, which is rude of them. The fern, to its credit, has never once been wrong about anything.

