Tamsin doesn't glance at the slip you leave. She slides it under the tally stone with the torn tag, squared to the edge. "Double toll," she says. "Paid by the ones who can't leave."

The stranger has shifted up the ration line, closer to the stall. His eyes are on you now. Tamsin lifts her pen and says, quietly, "He asked who you were."

