Tamsin's pen stays above the page. "Tide of cargo," she says, as if testing the weight of it. "Tides don't keep promises, but I keep ledgers." She taps the tally stone once. The stranger has crossed half the dock now, his boots loud on the plating. She turns the ledger toward you and says, "Then say it again where he can hear."

*Staking something real on that promise would be a Develop Your Relationship.*

