The Kobayashi IV slides into Bleakhold Station's docking cradle without a scrape. A clamp seats with a dull clang under your boots. Through the viewport, corporate-yellow lamps line the berths, each stamped with a company seal. A cargo clerk with a tablet is already walking the length of the berth, tapping something into it as he goes. He stops at your hull and writes down the ship's registry.

"Manifest to the dockmaster's window," he says, not looking up. "Before anything moves."

